<setup>
  <function name="v">0.25*x^3-1.5*x^2+3*x+0.25</function>
  <number name="L4">0.5*($$v(0)+$$v(0.5)+$$v(1)+$$v(1.5))</number>
  <number name="M4">0.5*($$v(0.25)+$$v(0.75)+$$v(1.25)+$$v(1.75))</number>
  <number name="R4">0.5*($$v(0.5)+$$v(1)+$$v(1.5)+$$v(2))</number>
</setup>


  <p>
    A person walking along a straight path has her velocity in miles per hour at time <m>t</m> given by the function <m>v(t) = 0.25t^3-1.5t^2+3t+0.25</m>,
    for times in the interval <m>0 \le t \le 2</m>.
    The graph of this function is also given in each of the three diagrams in the following figure.
  </p>

      <image width="85%" source="https://activecalculus.org/single2e/external/images/4_2_PA1.svg"><shortDescription>Three depictions of rectangles used to approximate area under the curve; the first uses left endpoints to calculate the heights of the rectangles, the second uses right endpoints, and the third uses midpoints.</shortDescription></image>
 
